/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (NFTs \(Non-Fungible Tokens\) are unique digital assets that represent ownership of items like art, music, virtual real estate, and collectibles, stored securely on blockchain networks. Unlike cryptocurrencies, each NFT is one of-a-kind and cannot be exchanged on a 1:1 basis. The global NFT market has grown rapidly, reaching a valuation of over $20 billion, fueled by demand in art, gaming, and the metaverse. NFT markets operate 24/7 across decentralized platforms, allowing users to mint, buy, sell, or trade tokens anytime. With blockchain backed authenticity and round-the-clock accessibility, NFTs are reshaping how digital ownership and value are defined in the digital economy)
